<h2 id="features">Features, placement and variants</h2>

The pinned frontend registers 53 feature types. The inventory maps each one to its domain contract. Render only the features and options the native card and entity support. Tile feature placement can be bottom or inline; moving a feature must preserve its label and reading order. A feature's configured mode list must not invent modes the device lacks.

| Feature family | Supported presentation variants to preserve | Local rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Climate, fan, humidifier and water-heater mode choices | Native dropdown or icon choices where that feature exposes them | Keep a text equivalent for every icon; use a dropdown when labels need room. |
| Select options | Dropdown or buttons | Display native option labels and retain the original stored value. |
| Numeric input, target temperature and target humidity | Buttons or slider | Keep bounds, steps and units; provide precise value entry where the native flow supports it. |
| Timer presets | Buttons or dropdown | A duration choice is not an elapsed timer reading. |
| Cover and valve favourites; light colour favourites | Supported named or value-based shortcuts | A favourite is a requested setting, not confirmation of current position or colour. |
| Bar gauge, trend and forecast | Read-only visualisations | Show quantity, period and a text value; never present a gauge as an adjustable slider. |

Do not turn every feature into a filled icon tile. Use one consistent MDI vocabulary for domain actions, 24px icons where appropriate, square surfaces, quiet dividers and the shared spacing scale. Retain domain colours only when their meaning is explained independently of colour.

