<h2 id="badges">Badges, headings, headers and footers</h2>

Entity and state-label badges summarise one identified state. Energy total badges need units and the selected period. Alert badges require the real alert meaning. Shortcut badges must name the destination. Entity-filter badges inherit the same empty/error distinction as filtered cards. An error badge is a failure state, not a generic warning icon.

Heading badges can show entity values or actions. Keep their accessible names meaningful outside the heading. Picture headers provide context; graph headers or footers need a matching summary; button headers or footers contain actual actions. Do not add decorative chart strips without a quantity and period. Preserve native support differences: not every card or view accepts every badge/header/footer.

